From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000219 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 02:25:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: require validated snapshot before owner
 registration

The state-owner lifecycle currently publishes the arbitration callbacks after
the identity check, even though identity alone does not prove that a complete
calibrated and live snapshot can be read coherently. Require the existing
read-only snapshot and validation callbacks to succeed before publishing the
owner registry callbacks, and clear the private callback object on every
failure path.

This is a fail-closed registration gate, not a provider. It performs no clock,
rail, EEM, secure, firmware, or CPU operation itself and remains uncalled by
the default profile. A real efuse/EEM/PPM/PMIC/clock provider and its external
transition lock are still required before CPU8 or CPU9 admission.
This patch is experiment-only and not submission-ready.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-state-owner-arbitration.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-state-owner-arbitration.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-state-owner-arbitration.c
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-state-owner-arbitration.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-state-owner-arbitration.c
@@ -309,5 +309,6 @@ int mt6797_dvfsp_state_owner_arbitration_register(
 	struct mt6797_dvfsp_handoff *handoff,
 	struct mt6797_dvfsp_state_owner_arbitration *arbitration)
 {
+	struct mt6797_dvfsp_state_snapshot snapshot;
 	int ret;
 
@@ -319,13 +320,22 @@ int mt6797_dvfsp_state_owner_arbitration_register(
 	ret = mt6797_dvfsp_state_owner_arbitration_owner_ops_init(
 		arbitration, &arbitration->owner_ops);
 	if (ret)
 		goto out_unlock;
+	memset(&snapshot, 0, sizeof(snapshot));
+	ret = mt6797_dvfsp_state_owner_arbitration_snapshot(
+		arbitration, &snapshot);
+	if (ret)
+		goto out_clear_ops;
+	ret = mt6797_dvfsp_state_owner_arbitration_validate(
+		arbitration, &snapshot);
+	if (ret)
+		goto out_clear_ops;
 	ret = mt6797_dvfsp_handoff_state_owner_register(
 		handoff, &arbitration->owner_ops, arbitration);
 	if (ret)
-		goto out_unlock;
+		goto out_clear_ops;
 
 	arbitration->handoff = handoff;
 	arbitration->registered = true;
+	goto out_unlock;
+
+out_clear_ops:
+	memset(&arbitration->owner_ops, 0, sizeof(arbitration->owner_ops));
 
 out_unlock:
 	mutex_unlock(&arbitration->lifecycle_lock);
-- 
